   {
    "pil": "FLSMTR",
    "text": "912 \nWGUS86 KMTR 250725\nFLSMTR\n\nFlood Advisory\nNational Weather Service San Francisco CA\n1125 PM PST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nCAC075-081-251030-\n/O.NEW.KMTR.FA.Y.0059.261125T0725Z-261125T1030Z/\n/00000.N.ER.000000T0000Z.000000T0000Z.000000T0000Z.OO/\nSan Francisco CA-San Mateo CA-\n1125 PM PST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\n...FLOOD ADVISORY IN EFFECT UNTIL 230 AM PST WEDNESDAY...\n\n* WHAT...Urban area caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southern San Francisco County in northern California...\n  Northwestern San Mateo County in northern California...\n\n* WHEN...Until 230 AM PST.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n  Ponding of water in urban or other areas is occurring or is\n  imminent.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n  - At 1124 PM PST, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain. This will\n    cause urban and small stream flooding.\n  - Some locations that will experience flooding include...\n    Daly City, South San Francisco, San Bruno, Pacifica, Burlingame,\n    Millbrae, Hillsborough, Brisbane, Colma, Broadmoor and Montara.\n  - Rainfall rates are between 0.25 to 0.75 inches per hour.\n  - http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood\n\nPRECAUTIONARY/PREPAREDNESS ACTIONS...\n\nTurn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.\n\n&&\n\nLAT...LON 3771 12250 3771 12239 3767 12238 3766 12240\n      3767 12237 3764 12240 3764 12238 3763 12239\n      3763 12237 3761 12236 3761 12238 3759 12235\n      3759 12236 3758 12235 3756 12234 3754 12252\n      3760 12252 3761 12250\n\n\n$$\n\nKR\n\n\u0003"
   },
   {
    "pil": "FLSMTR",
    "text": "311 \nWGUS86 KMTR 250701\nFLSMTR\n\nFlood Advisory\nNational Weather Service San Francisco CA\n1101 PM PST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nCAC075-251000-\n/O.NEW.KMTR.FA.Y.0058.261125T0701Z-261125T1000Z/\n/00000.N.ER.000000T0000Z.000000T0000Z.000000T0000Z.OO/\nSan Francisco CA-\n1101 PM PST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\n...FLOOD ADVISORY IN EFFECT UNTIL 2 AM PST WEDNESDAY...\n\n* WHAT...Urban area flooding caused by excessive rainfall is\n  expected.\n\n* WHERE...San Francisco County in northern California...\n\n* WHEN...Until 200 AM PST.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n  Ponding of water in urban or other areas is occurring or is\n  imminent.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n  - At 1059 PM PST, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain. This will\n    cause urban flooding. Overflowing poor drainage areas will cause\n    minor flooding in the advisory area.\n  - Rainfall rates of 0.25 to 0.80 inches have been observed.\n  - Some locations that will experience flooding include...\n    San Francisco.\n  - http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood\n\nPRECAUTIONARY/PREPAREDNESS ACTIONS...\n\nTurn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.\n\n&&\n\nLAT...LON 3778 12252 3779 12249 3781 12248 3781 12241\n      3779 12239 3775 12238 3775 12239 3774 12238\n      3773 12238 3773 12236 3772 12236 3772 12239\n      3771 12238 3771 12250\n\n\n$$\n\nSarment\n\n\u0003"
